 Also called: Global Voxel Clustering
 ## Overview
-Voxel Clustering (Global) is a preprocessing step in volume rendering that groups downsampled voxels into a small number of clusters based on their albedo values to share weight factors for scattering parameters [S1]. It addresses the challenge of managing a large number of unknowns in anisotropic media rendering by reducing spatial variability into discrete, globally consistent groups [S1]. Unlike sibling methods that may handle local or illumination-specific variations, this method operates on the entire volume's albedo distribution to minimize global rendering error [S1].
